{{smaller block|Calculations so difficult as to have ''baffled'' . . . the most enlightened nations.
{{right|''Prescott.''}}
I never watched Robert in my life but my scrutiny was presently ''baffled'' by finding he was watching me.
{{right|''Charlotte Brontë'', Shirley, xv.}}}}

'''4.''' To beat about, as the wind or stray cattle do standing grain or grass; twist irregularly together. {{smaller|='''Syn. 3.''' ''Foil'', ''Thwart'', etc. See ''frustrate''.}}

